WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:11.060
Traceability allows organizations to connect software changes to developers, reviews, tickets, approvals, builds, tests, artifacts, and deployments.

2
00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:18.140
When a change can be traced from idea to production, teams gain visibility into the software delivery lifecycle.

3
00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:25.280
That visibility helps with incident review, defect analysis, customer questions, and audit response.

4
00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:29.960
Practical traceability often depends on consistent identifiers.

5
00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:40.700
A ticket reference in a branch name, commit, pull request, build record, and deployment record can connect separate tools into one accountable story.

6
00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:44.500
Traceability should also include the deployed artifact.

7
00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:51.960
Teams should be able to identify which source revision produced an artifact, which checks it passed, who approved it, and where it was deployed.
